"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: accepted the grounded G1G2 finding. The plan now explicitly cites T15 in the packaged guide, regenerates the criterion-pins manifest, validates it through the real test_guides and test_guide_criterion_pins suites, and runs registry validate-routing. File impact now includes the generated pin manifest and the guide rendering contract. Also resolved the observed hand-authored gate-doc enumeration precisely: update T1–T12 to T1–T15 and align the adjacent criterion count with registry validation.","timestamp":1786564880667505001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED evidence: worktree-venv run collected and executed the complete four-test oracle; all four failed for the intended missing behavior. The supported explain_guide and real `rebar explain plan` subprocess lack T15 and its local-or-manual/scoped-cleanup guidance, and docs/plan-review-gate.md still says 32 criteria / T1–T12. The earlier ambient-Python import error was discarded as invalid environment evidence. Oracle contract: authoritative sources are this ticket plus the shipped T15 rubric; production path is packaged guide -> explain_guide -> CLI; exact postconditions are rendered T15 guidance, stack-agnostic cleanup boundary, and current 44/T1–T15 hand-authored docs; CI gate is make test. No state, recovery, or contention mechanism applies.","timestamp":1786565359626800001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out validation: implementer reported 3 attempts and saw only the one visible happy-path test. Restored edge/E2E oracle initially produced two whitespace-sensitive false failures; under revert-first discipline I removed the implementation, normalized rendered Markdown whitespace in those tests, reconfirmed all four tests RED for the true missing T15/count behavior, restored the unchanged implementation, and all four passed. Defect-seeded mutation removed the scoped-cleanup contract; the held-out edge test went RED on the missing `only the resources it created` consequence, then GREEN after restoration. Tests assert public explain_guide/CLI output and hand-authored docs, not private structure.","timestamp":1786565595928480001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Preflight complete. Held-out TDD: 4/4 oracle failures at RED, 4/4 GREEN after implementation; mutation removing the scoped-cleanup guidance was killed. Focused guide/pin suite: 37 passed. Criteria routing validation: 44 criteria in sync. git diff --check, make lint, and make typecheck all passed. Full suite: 12,368 passed, 62 skipped, 264 deselected, 38 warnings in 47m21s. Local review-code capability is disabled in this checkout, so no local LLM code-review verdict was available; Gerrit LLM-Review remains authoritative.","timestamp":1786568550357052001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Rebased cleanly onto origin/main 3ada40862d; no incoming file overlapped this patch. Post-rebase gates: 37 focused guide/pin tests passed in 31.43s; criteria_routing.json parity OK (44 criteria); make lint passed; make typecheck passed (512 source files); git diff --check passed; verify-commit-ticket resolved canonical 3192-a652-0368-42c2. Commit f565a29a33d58c7ca0323a964782f3aba63fa70b carries DCO sign-off and Change-Id I789262874819437bdd5e8e1e8666f9688107ea37.","timestamp":1786568678623166001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Addressed all three Gerrit LLM-review advisories in patchset 2. The two overlapping count/range findings are resolved by deriving the expected criterion cardinality and T-overlay bounds from CANONICAL_LLM before comparing them to the hand-authored doc. The fixed 1000-character T15 slice is replaced by a reusable Markdown bullet-boundary helper, so product-name negative checks cannot bleed into adjacent guidance. Rebased cleanly onto origin/main 104dc4e10a (incoming commit had no file overlap). Refreshed gates: 37 focused tests passed; make lint passed; make typecheck passed (512 files); diff check and canonical trailer verification passed.","timestamp":1786569147999798001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit patchset 2 CI upstream blocker: run 31641453023 packaging/provenance/identity/ticket/golden-path jobs passed, but all three completed pytest matrix jobs failed before pytest at the base complexity lock. Exact reproduction on current origin/main 104dc4e10a: close_ticket ceiling raised 17 -> 19. This story changes only docs/plan-review-gate.md, the packaged guide/pins, and test_guides.py. Recorded the unrelated base regression as priority-1 bug humble-cinnamoned-mussel (657a-47a3-436f-4a16); no ceiling raise or unrelated fix will be folded into this story.","timestamp":1786569538409285001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final Gerrit advisory addressed under refreshed signed plan: registry.py module docstring now states the validated 44 / T1-T15 vocabulary, and the guide test derives count/range from CANONICAL_LLM and checks both gate docs and registry docstring. Rebased cleanly onto origin/main 07e76a1ce3; incoming commits had no file overlap. The upstream close_ticket extraction is now on main, so the exact previously failing CI precheck passes: complexity-baseline lock OK. Post-rebase: 37 focused tests passed, make lint passed, make typecheck passed (513 files), diff check and canonical trailer verification passed.","timestamp":1786570521234955001}],"created_at":1784918875620810001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"80ea6fba-bcea-48bc-bd38-d7afa6000f90","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ea28-020e-8215-4eb9"},{"link_uuid":"163eac54-7c6d-4392-ae1a-b9d7ce93c31b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c4c6-a050-59ab-45c7"},{"link_uuid":"df76a83d-53b4-4569-9d41-ef658541fd3d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2137-be2f-cb5b-48b0"}],"description":"Update the author-facing documentation so writers know to de-risk risky runtime mechanisms out-of-loop before committing them to a slow delivery loop — the behavior T15 rewards.\n\n## Work\n- Edit `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`, surfaced by `rebar explain plan`, to explain that when correctness only resolves after a slow codified delivery loop such as CI/CD, IaC apply, or provisioning, the plan names the risky mechanisms and commits to a concrete fast out-of-loop proof before codifying.\n- Identify the new packaged-guide guidance as T15 so authors can find the corresponding rubric.\n- State that the proof is either a local run or a manual probe against the real target.\n- State that throwaway experiments are cleaned up with teardown scoped only to resources they created.\n- Because the packaged guide will cite T15, regenerate `src/rebar/_guides/criterion-pins.json` with `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.guide_parity regenerate`.\n- Update the hand-authored overlay enumeration in `docs/plan-review-gate.md` from the stale T1–T12 range to T1–T15 and align its stated criterion count with the validated registry. The generated criteria guide itself is owned by the criterion story, not this story.\n- Keep all guidance stack-agnostic; CI/CD, IaC apply, and provisioning are mechanism classes, not product-specific instructions.\n\n- Update the stale registry module docstring in src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py from 32 / T1–T12 to the validated 44 / T1–T15 vocabulary, keeping the implementation authority aligned with the author-facing docs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` renders guidance to name risky mechanisms whose correctness resolves only after a slow codified delivery loop.\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` identifies the new guidance as T15.\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` renders the two permitted fast proof forms: a local run or a manual probe against the real target.\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` renders cleanup guidance that limits teardown to resources created by the throwaway experiment.\n- [ ] The new guidance does not hardcode Terraform, Docker, or another product-specific stack.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_guides/criterion-pins.json` contains the regenerated T15 pin for the packaged plan guide.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` describes the triggered overlay range as T1–T15.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` states the criterion count reported by registry validation.\n- [ ] Existing `rebar explain plan` guide rendering remains intact outside the new guidance.\n\n- [ ] The registry module docstring states the same validated criterion count and T-overlay range as docs/plan-review-gate.md.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `.venv/bin/rebar explain plan` and verify the rendered T15 slow-loop, local-or-manual-proof, and scoped-cleanup guidance.\n- Run `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_guides.py tests/unit/test_guide_criterion_pins.py -q` to prove the packaged guide renders through the supported explain surface and the generated pin manifest is current.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry validate-routing` and confirm the reported registry count matches `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n- Inspect the changed prose to confirm it contains no product-specific Terraform or Docker instruction.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md","reason":"T15 de-risk guidance surfaced by rebar explain plan"},{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/criterion-pins.json","reason":"regenerated packaged-guide criterion pin manifest for the new T15 citation"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"T15 overlay range and validated criterion-count consistency"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py","reason":"align the registry module docstring with the validated 44 / T1-T15 vocabulary"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_guides.py","reason":"observable packaged-guide rendering and live-registry documentation contracts"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","ea28-020e-8215-4eb9"],["parent","8fc2-0306-a9a0-4864"],["relates_to","2137-be2f-cb5b-48b0"],["relates_to","c4c6-a050-59ab-45c7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"8fc2-0306-a9a0-4864","parent_status_uuid":"d2e56ba7-963f-4c53-bb94-ff7e36a8fe7c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3192-a652-0368-42c2","ticket_type":"story","title":"Update writing-a-passing-plan guide + gate docs for de-risk-before-slow-loop","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6d834553-0e31-48c0-b1e3-90faa84cc699","523bb625-32ea-4069-9fe9-afcf6671d5e9","c6cb3f2e-75a9-447b-a57a-8e57461847ef","80ea6fba-bcea-48bc-bd38-d7afa6000f90","8f765da0-09cd-45d2-ae28-8a94c77232cc","97439bfa-9ef5-4765-bf94-1b629e75691e","f30eb14b-67f0-4ff1-8a2f-2db276e666e8","1805db07-435b-4aae-860a-8feacc9850a9","b3abc64d-e2d1-402f-bc91-dcd2b7985430","d2e56ba7-963f-4c53-bb94-ff7e36a8fe7c","3bd9e322-45ec-47fd-93b9-9201b4f05a89","511eb7ce-0f58-4999-b2dd-4ca9179139e4","7a8fef08-2308-4f4a-8f97-fddcb8aa1dec","55f83526-dd2c-4724-b13d-d2ca5a694098","3ed1ce9a-8719-4912-b700-eebca251644d","163eac54-7c6d-4392-ae1a-b9d7ce93c31b","a3e68642-c3cf-4d8c-ab33-c5fad6fd13f2","8c497c24-ee0b-4406-99cc-bd340a0eecaf","df76a83d-53b4-4569-9d41-ef658541fd3d","904bb764-214c-4a18-ab52-7f4abe795f83","1d08a22a-82a7-4a8f-962c-2efb7c70f8d7","44989dc0-ccf6-4140-99b4-f75aadcf9b86","b7d3d013-652c-4471-a984-b46d1e7e6bce"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786570521234955002,"uuid":"33236319-1711-4869-8486-abeedb1abfa6"}